    "question": "A 40 meters rope was cut into 2 parts in the ratio of 2:3. How long is the shorter part?",
    "gold": "16",
    "answer": "The rope was cut into 2 + 3 = <<2+3=5>>5 parts.\nSo each part is 40/5 = <<40/5=8>>8 meters long.\nSince the shorter part is consists of 2 parts, then it is 8 x 2 = <<8*2=16>>16 meters long.\n#### 16"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the length of the shorter part of the rope, we start by understanding the ratio given, which is 2:3. This means that for every 2 parts of the rope, there are 3 parts. The total number of parts is the sum of the parts in the ratio, which is \\(2 + 3 = 5\\).\n\nThe total length of the rope is 40 meters. To find the length of one part, we divide the total length by the total number of parts:\n\\[\n\\text{Length of one part} = \\frac{40 \\text{ meters}}{5} = 8 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nThe shorter part of the rope corresponds to 2 parts. Therefore, the length of the shorter part is:\n\\[\n\\text{Length of the shorter part} = 2 \\times 8 \\text{ meters} = 16 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of the shorter part of the rope is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
